## Summary

Consistency audit of main at 134a42a7 (the "Audit" workflow's Consistency stage). It set out to make the codebase consistent with its own rules: one dialect and one name per concept in user-facing words, docs that match the code, comments and code style within AGENTS.md's rules.

Found: the Go code already met every rule checked (no comments beyond two-line subtle-logic notes, `any` everywhere, lowercase slog messages, braces on every body, `make` only for lengths and channels, double-dash flags). What fell short was the docs. Changed, docs and comments only, no behavior:

- Stale doc statements fixed against the code. README.md's Layout listed `internal/static`, which no longer exists, described `internal/blob` as an in-memory media cache with thumbnails (it is the plain Cloud Storage layer with no cache), and omitted 15 internal packages, now each listed with a verified one-liner. docs/deploy.md described a blob-store prefetch at startup, a 256 MiB `dataBudget` cache, a `birthdayBase` constant and boot log lines that no longer exist; its min-instances, memory and startup-log paragraphs and the `gcloud logging read` filter now name what the server does and logs today. docs/dev.md named ten testkit helpers that do not exist; it now names the real exports. docs/who/directory.md pointed at `familyNameFor` and a `shortName` field; it now points at the `familyName` trigger and Who?'s `familyShortName`. `policySource` became `PolicySource` in three docs. docs/audits/code.md dropped `mail.ICSEscape`. docs/who/pwa.md lost the bullet allowing a service worker, which the project never uses.
- American English throughout the docs and three stylesheets' comments (about 75 words: colour, grey, centred, labelled, licence, behaviour, neighbour, travelling), because the code, the schema's `color` column and the UI's own strings are American and the project states no dialect.
- "Sign in" as the one term: docs/screenshots.md's "Log in"/"logins" and Helios Who?'s manifest description "Please log in with…".
- One garbled CSS comment in web/when/style.css fixed.

Method: a scratchpad checker that extracted every backticked path and identifier from the docs and looked for it in the code, then verifying each miss by hand; rg scans for comments, dialect words, log and error message style, braceless bodies and single-dash flags.

Deliberately left out: `cancelled`, the schema's enum value, keeps its spelling; Claude prompts with "summarise"/"organised" are behavior; button-label capitalization is split evenly between Title Case and sentence case (Helios When has both "Make Default"/"Make default" and "Send Now"/"Send now") with no stated rule, so it was reported as a design decision for ian rather than changed; the hundreds of descriptive section comments in every app's style.css break the no-comments rule but mislead nobody, so they stayed; test-only strings and the `labelled` parameter name are not user-facing; `team-admins` in docs/team is a production-data statement the sample data cannot confirm.

The final merge-in of main (four commits from the other audit stages and the Helios Admin logo) was clean with no conflicts; `go vet ./...` and the auth and app package tests passed.

